## 6. DEMOSTRACIONES COMPLETAS DEL LIBRO HOLLANDER & WOLFE

### 6.1 Demostración: E(T⁺) = n(n+1)/4 y V(T⁺) = n(n+1)(2n+1)/24

**Método:** Variables indicadoras V_i

Definir V_i = i si la observación con rango i es positiva, 0 si es negativa.
Bajo H₀: P(V_i = i) = 1/2, P(V_i = 0) = 1/2
T⁺ = ΣV_i

**Esperanza:**
E(V_i) = i(1/2) + 0(1/2) = i/2
E(T⁺) = ΣE(V_i) = Σi/2 = (1/2)[n(n+1)/2] = n(n+1)/4 ✓

**Varianza:**
E(V_i²) = i²(1/2) + 0²(1/2) = i²/2
V(V_i) = E(V_i²) - [E(V_i)]² = i²/2 - (i/2)² = i²/4
V(T⁺) = ΣV(V_i) = Σi²/4 = (1/4)[n(n+1)(2n+1)/6] = n(n+1)(2n+1)/24 ✓

### 6.2 Demostración: T⁺ + T⁻ = n(n+1)/2

T⁺ = ΣR_iψ_i, T⁻ = ΣR_i(1-ψ_i)
T⁺ + T⁻ = ΣR_i[ψ_i + (1-ψ_i)] = ΣR_i = 1+2+...+n = n(n+1)/2 ✓

### 6.3 Demostración: E(W) = n(N+1)/2, V(W) = mn(N+1)/12

**Método:** Muestreo sin reemplazo de población finita

Bajo H₀, los rangos de las Y's son una muestra aleatoria de tamaño n de {1,2,...,N}.
μ_pop = (N+1)/2
σ²_pop = (N²-1)/12 = (N-1)(N+1)/12

E(W/n) = μ_pop = (N+1)/2 → E(W) = n(N+1)/2 ✓
V(W/n) = (σ²_pop/n)((N-n)/(N-1)) = [(N+1)(N-1)/(12n)] [(N-n)/(N-1)] = m(N+1)/(12n)
V(W) = n² V(W/n) = mn(N+1)/12 ✓

### 6.4 Demostración: Relación W = U + n(n+1)/2

R(Y_j) = #X's < Y_j + #Y's < Y_j + 1
ΣR(Y_j) = Σ_iΣ_j φ(X_i,Y_j) + Σ_jΣ_j' φ(Y_j',Y_j) + n
El primer término es U, el segundo es 0+1+...+(n-1) = n(n-1)/2
W = U + n(n-1)/2 + n = U + n(n+1)/2 ✓

### 6.5 Demostración: R(f'') = 3/(8σ⁵√π)

f(x) = (1/(σ√(2π))) exp(-(x-μ)²/(2σ²))
z = (x-μ)/σ, dx = σdz

f'(x) = -(z/σ)f(x)
f''(x) = ((z²-1)/σ²)f(x) = ((z²-1)/(σ²)) (1/(σ√(2π))) e^(-z²/2)

R(f'') = ∫(f''(x))²dx = (1/(σ⁵2π)) ∫(z²-1)²e^(-z²)dz
= (1/(σ⁵2π)) [∫z⁴e^(-z²)dz - 2∫z²e^(-z²)dz + ∫e^(-z²)dz]
= (1/(σ⁵2π)) [(3√π/4) - 2(√π/2) + √π]
= (1/(σ⁵2π)) [3√π/4] = 3/(8σ⁵√π) ✓

### 6.6 Demostración: h óptimo = 1.059σn^(-1/5)

AMISE = R(K)/(nh) + (σ_K⁴h⁴/4)R(f'')
∂AMISE/∂h = -R(K)/(nh²) + σ_K⁴h³R(f'') = 0
h_opt = [R(K)/(nσ_K⁴R(f''))]^(1/5)

Con K gaussiano (σ_K²=1, R(K)=1/(2√π)) y f normal (R(f'')=3/(8σ⁵√π)):
h_opt = [(1/(2√π))/(n·1·3/(8σ⁵√π))]^(1/5) = (4σ⁵/(3n))^(1/5) = (4/3)^(1/5)σn^(-1/5) ≈ 1.059σn^(-1/5) ✓

### 6.7 Demostración: Varianza del Estimador Kernel (para normal)

V(f̂_K(x)) = (1/n)[φ(x; μ, σ²+2h²) - (φ(x; μ, σ²+h²))²]

**Demostración (esbozo):**
V(f̂_K(x)) = (1/n)[E(K_h²(x-X)) - (E(K_h(x-X)))²]
Para X ~ N(μ, σ²) y K gaussiano:
E(K_h(x-X)) = φ(x; μ, σ²+h²)
E(K_h²(x-X)) = φ(x; μ, σ²+2h²) (usando convolución)
Sustituyendo se obtiene el resultado. ✓

