## 8. RESOLUCIÓN DETALLADA DEL PARCIAL 1 (I-2026)

### 8.1 Punto 1: Teoría (40%)

**1. Demuestre que f̂_H(x) = f̂_K(x), con K(u) = 1/2, u ∈ [-1,1]**

f̂_H(x) = (1/(nb)) Σ (1/2) I_[-1,1]((x_i-x)/b)
f̂_K(x) = (1/(nh)) Σ K((x-x_i)/h)
Con K(u) = (1/2)I_[-1,1](u) y h=b:
f̂_K(x) = (1/(nb)) Σ (1/2) I_[-1,1]((x-x_i)/b) = f̂_H(x) ✓

**2. Demuestre que E(f̂_K(x)) ≈ f(x) + f''(x)σ_K²h²/2**

E(f̂_K(x)) = ∫(1/h)K((x-t)/h)f(t)dt
u = (x-t)/h, t = x-hu, dt = -hdu
= ∫K(u)f(x-hu)du
Taylor: f(x-hu) = f(x) - f'(x)hu + (1/2)f''(x)h²u² + O(h³)
= f(x)∫K(u)du - f'(x)h∫uK(u)du + (1/2)f''(x)h²∫u²K(u)du + O(h³)
= f(x) + 0 + (1/2)f''(x)h²σ_K² + O(h³) ✓

**3. Demuestre que V(f̂_K(x)) ≈ f(x)R(K)/(nh)**

V(f̂_K(x)) = (1/n²)ΣV((1/h)K((x-X_i)/h)) = (1/n)V((1/h)K((x-X)/h))
= (1/n)[E((1/h²)K²((x-X)/h)) - (E((1/h)K((x-X)/h)))²]
E((1/h²)K²((x-X)/h)) = ∫(1/h²)K²((x-t)/h)f(t)dt = (1/h)∫K²(u)f(x-hu)du ≈ f(x)R(K)/h
V ≈ (1/n)(f(x)R(K)/h) = f(x)R(K)/(nh) ✓

**4. Deduzca MISE, AMISE, h óptimo, h referencia normal**

MISE = ∫[V + Sesgo²]dx = ∫[f(x)R(K)/(nh) + (f''(x)σ_K²h²/2)²]dx
= R(K)/(nh) + (σ_K⁴h⁴/4)R(f'')

AMISE = R(K)/(nh) + (σ_K⁴h⁴/4)R(f'')

h_opt: ∂AMISE/∂h = -R(K)/(nh²) + σ_K⁴h³R(f'') = 0
h_opt = [R(K)/(nσ_K⁴R(f''))]^(1/5)

Con K gaussiano y f normal: h_opt = 1.059σn^(-1/5)

**5. Demuestre IC para √E(f̂(x)) y dé IC para E(f̂(x))**

Método Delta: g(t) = √t, g'(t) = 1/(2√t)
√f̂_K(x) ~ N(√E(f̂_K(x)), (1/(4E(f̂_K(x))))·(f(x)R(K)/(nh)))
≈ N(√E(f̂_K(x)), R(K)/(4nh)) (asumiendo E≈f)
IC: [√f̂_K(x) ± Z_(α/2)√(R(K)/(4nh))]
IC para E(f̂(x)): [(√f̂_K(x) - Z√(R(K)/(4nh)))², (√f̂_K(x) + Z√(R(K)/(4nh)))²]

